Where the f*** did you get that from?

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.520
Everybody's favourite Gary Brannan,
Gary Brannan.

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:31.000
♪ Trailer for sale or rent,
underpants like a tent. ♪

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.160
And the bounciest man on the internet,
Matt Gray.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:39.840
Please let us know if you spot the secret
shamanist message in this show.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:40.720
" 'Eezer goode."

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:42.680
Oh! F*** that.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:50.280
That is the most reluctant clap
I have ever heard for an introduction.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:52.240
Matt, they're going to sound like
they're at gunpoint.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:56.000
In front of me, I've got an article from
Wikipedia and these folks can't see it.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:57.880
Every fact they get right is a point and a ding

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:00.680
and there's a special prize
for particularly good answers which is:

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:04.400
Oh, they're in tune tonight.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:08.120
And today we are talking about a hail cannon.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.040
Is it a cannon that shoots hail?

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:11.520
No.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:13.880
Did this belong to Ming the Merciless?

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:17.520
"Klytus, I'm bored.
What plaything can you offer me today?"

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:19.680
"A vibrator, or a cannon that shoots hail."

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:22.720
Are you using those for the same thing?

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:23.640
Because wow.

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:26.120
I was about to say,
that's a very weird version of Flash Gordon

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:29.640
but there literally is a parody of…
of Flash Gordon.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:31.320
-That would be Flesh Gordon.
-Yes.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.880
Which went around at my school like hotcakes,
let me tell you.

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:35.960
The hail cannon does not shoot hail.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:38.840
Is it a "meteorological event"?

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:40.800
-Ooh!
-Why did I say that like Michael Gambon?

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:43.600
"Izzita-meteorological-event?"

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:45.040
Is it something like cloud seeding?

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:45.920
Ooh.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:49.320
So a hail cannon might be something you set off
from a plane into the clouds

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:50.320
to make hail happen.

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:52.360
[TOGETHER] Why would you want that?

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:01.720
Now in stereo.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:09.240
I'm giving…
I'm giving biscuits there for two reasons.

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:13.960
First, stereo,
and secondly, that is a very good question.

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:18.040
The hail cannon does not create hailstones,
you wouldn't want that.

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:18.960
What would you want?

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:21.360
Does it stop hailstones?
Does it slush them?

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:27.160
It is a shockwave generator
claimed to disrupt the formation of hailstones.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:29.600
Ooh! Ooh!

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:31.240
You look surprised by this, Chris.

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:33.240
-No.
-Either that or you've just sat on yourself.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:36.200
"Ooh, me hailstones!"

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:38.840
Well, they've been shattered.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:43.520
Was this first discovered when Brian Blessed
climbed Mount Everest

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:46.200
in that a loud enough shockwave
which shatter water?

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.320
"Stop that, I'm camping!"

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:52.680
Oh, it's just a big bang, so it is just a
cannon that makes a big loud thing,

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:55.760
and then the big loud thing makes the hail go,
"No, I'm not going to be hail anymore."

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:56.560
Apparently, yes.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:57.880
What, 'I'm going back up'?

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:02.560
It just looks like a big cone with a box
at the bottom of it.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:03.680
What do they put in the box?

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:06.360
A man's part, then slam the lid shut.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:09.080
Oh! Oh, that'll get a loud noise, that would.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:10.400
That would get a very loud noise.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:11.820
Acetylene and oxygen.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:14.200
Hang on a minute, is this farting into clouds?

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.240
I've talked about this before.

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:18.600
-I still think it was a good...
-Yes, but you meant you had your arse

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:20.840
against a plane window
and were hoping for the best.

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:23.520
Yeah, but in the service of humanity.

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:27.100
It's basically a contained
'boomph' of an explosion,

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:29.920
And then all that force gets projected
up into the sky.

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:31.440
-It's a airzooka.
-Yeah.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:34.400
I'm being hesitant about saying
that's what it's doing.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:35.880
Has no one ever actually done it?

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:37.380
Lots of people have done it.

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:39.880
These are installed in a lot of places.

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:41.560
Has no one measured their success?

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:46.120
-I mean…
-"Never been cited in a peer reviewed journal."

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:48.960
Oh, just because it's never hailed
after that's happened

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:50.680
doesn't mean it was going to hail
to begin with.

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:54.800
Because you can't tell.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:56.880
There has been a review,

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:59.720
which is why I didn't give you a point for
'Has no one done the research?'

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:01.640
They have done the research
and the results were...?

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:03.240
Inconclusive.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:04.560
No, pretty conclusive.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:05.880
-Didn't work?
-Yes.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:10.160
People are firing massive amounts

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:12.600
of explosive gases in the air
to create a massive boom,

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:14.440
for no f***ing reason at all.

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:15.840
-Yes.
-I love our race.

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:18.320
There is another reason to doubt it.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.960
What else happens near hailstorms

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:23.360
that would be a heck of a lot more powerful
than one of these cannons?

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:24.840
Brian Blessed, skydiving.

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:27.320
-Planes?
-Thunderbolts and lightning.

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:29.380
-Correct.
[TOGETHER] -Very, very frightening.

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:30.160
F***!

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:41.080
At least that one was vaguely scripted.

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:45.880
Which does bring me to something
called a cloud buster.

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:48.280
Oh, now, this was a song by Kate Bush.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:51.960
Oh! Oh! Gary.

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:53.040
Thank you.

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:58.440
It was, this was the device that inspired
the Kate Bush song, Cloudbusting.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:01.240
'I'm running up that hill, I'm something,
something, something else,'

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:05.760
but it's about the man runs up a hill and is he
like a scientist who's arrested at the end?

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:08.080
I'm remembering the video
more than the actual facts here.

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:12.480
You say scientist,
the man's name was Wilhelm Reich.

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:14.800
He was Austrian and a psychoanalyst.

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:17.520
So not innately qualified to do weather.

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:19.360
No. No.

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:21.960
And the cloud buster
wasn't like the hail cannon.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:24.280
It had a very different intent.

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:25.320
To make it rain?

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:28.760
To make it rain by doing what?

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:31.920
Did they lob dogs named Buster
up into the clouds?

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:36.920
Did they lob copies of the 1980s film about the
Great Train Robbery, 'Buster', into the air?

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:38.840
-Do you want to be the third one on this, Chris...
-No.

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:39.960
No, okay.

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:41.200
Okay. No.

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:45.760
It was a series of parallel hollow metal tubes
at the end.

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:46.920
Tubular bells?

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:50.920
Flexible hoses
and then those are placed in water.

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:52.960
Is he shooting water into a cloud
to make it rain?

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:54.960
No, I've just described the entire thing,
you've got…

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:57.000
-It's just a thing sat there?
-Some tubes, some hoses

00:05:57.000 --> 00:06:01.800
and some water and it claims to manipulate
something called orgone energy.

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:04.580
Oh!

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:05.800
It's bollocks.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:06.880
Yes, it is.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:14.880
O-R-G-O-N-E, it might be 'org-own' or 'org-on'.

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:17.440
It literally has a mark in Wikipedia here,
it says

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:19.520
'Orgone: pronunciation?'

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:21.600
No one knows.

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:24.440
And then it says it is a pseudoscientific concept

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:28.000
and there are seven references
after the word 'pseudoscientific'.

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:29.480
There's been some arguments here.

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:30.480
Officially bollocks.

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:32.560
What is orgone energy supposed to be?

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:36.600
It's the chi version but for weather.

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:38.000
Oh, it's a bit further than that.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:40.040
Is it supposed to be the equivalent
of whatever dark matter is?

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:43.560
Is it some kind of surrounding force
that holds water in?

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:45.960
It's actually, it's not just to do with water.

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:48.240
Is it a life force, is it a binding life force?

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:50.640
Yes, it is essentially
the Force from Star Wars.

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:56.520
It is an esoteric energy,
a hypothetical universal life force.

00:06:56.520 --> 00:07:03.360
And by putting a vibraphone into some water
via some hoses, I can make the Force cry.

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:08.400
What you have done there, Gary,
is just give the best…

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:11.480
the best summing up of the cloud buster
that I think I've ever heard.

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:13.120
(Kate Bush, call me.)

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:15.960
This is moving back now to actually trying
to make rain.

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:20.680
This is not orgone and the cloud buster,
this is the US military.

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:26.080
And they created Operation Popeye,
1967 to 1972.

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:28.880
Any ideas where that might have been?

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:30.760
-Vietnam.
-Yes, absolutely right.

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:35.760
Why might the US military during
the Vietnam War, have wanted to make rain?

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:38.880
-Is this Napalm?
-No. No, this is literal rain.

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:42.240
Is it to kind of drive them out of the jungle
because it's so very wet,

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:44.120
-and horrible and they don't like it anymore?
-No.

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:47.640
Is it to wash off all the Agent Orange
that they've used to poison the entire country?

00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:48.360
Ooh.

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:50.560
Is it to get Agent Orange into the rainfall

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:52.640
and then use that to drop it
rather than the aeroplanes?

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:56.880
No, it's actually,
it's more of a tactic about logistics.

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:58.080
Well, to make the roads muddy?

00:07:58.080 --> 00:07:59.520
-Yes.
-So they can't move things around.

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:03.800
Yes, soften the road surfaces,
cause landslides, wash out river crossings.

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:06.800
And one other thing
about the climate in Vietnam.

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:08.960
-Make it very humid and therefore…
-It already is.

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:10.880
-It already is, isn't it?
-What happens there,

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:12.880
-about certain times of the year?
-Monsoon season.

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:21.300
Yes. The idea was to extend monsoon season,
with the 54th Weather Reconnaissance Squadron.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:25.680
Who had a slogan, and it was, it ended with the
words 'Not war'.

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:27.640
-What were the first two?
-Make rain.

00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:30.200
'Make something, not war.'

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:32.120
-Water.
-Wet?

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:35.800
Okay, you've got the rain,
you've got the ground, you put them together.

00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:37.000
Slippery.

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:39.840
-Make slippery, not war?
-Yes.

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:42.360
Yes, sounds perfectly reasonable to me.

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:44.760
'Make mud, not war' was their slogan.

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:46.600
But weren't they making mud to make war?

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:48.120
-Yes.
-No!

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:53.380
They conducted 50 experiments in the
Laos Panhandle.

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:55.600
And the government of Laos,
what did they think about this?

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:58.280
Did they not even notice
because nothing happened?

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:03.080
You're close, but no.

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:06.040
Were they annoyed that they were flying about
all that and then nothing happened?

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:09.880
-No. No, they weren't annoyed by it at all.
-Did they like it because it watered their crops-

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:11.600
-No, they didn't like it either.
-Did they notice?

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:13.680
They weren't actually even told about it.

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:16.160
-Cheeky.
-The US government just decided to fly over

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:21.000
and seed some clouds with lead iodide
and silver iodide.

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:22.840
Oh! Oh, they're bad.

00:09:22.840 --> 00:09:24.280
-They are.
-Purple rain?

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:27.840
Bloody Prince again.

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:29.560
Isn't iodine purple?

00:09:29.560 --> 00:09:30.640
Yes.

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:33.400
I've never listened to the lyrics
of Purple Rain before.

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:36.200
Neither have I and I'm rapidly thinking,
are they about this now?

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:37.920
No, no, no, they're not. No.

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:39.640
Wait, I'm going to check that.

00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:47.640
Because let me… let me tell you,
if it turns out purple rain,

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:51.120
is actually about the US military's
cloud seeding experiments in Laos,

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:52.560
I am giving you biscuits.

00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:56.800
Prince explained the meaning of Purple Rain
as follows,

00:09:56.800 --> 00:10:00.180
"when there's blood in the sky,
red and blue equals purple".

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:04.360
So unfortunately, no, it's not about
the US military seeding with lead iodide.

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:06.960
But it could have been.

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:08.280
Yeah, sure.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:11.460
Also I'm fairly sure lead iodide
is not actually purple.

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:14.360
No, as soon as you change iodine into something
else it would lose it's colour, wouldn't it?

00:10:14.360 --> 00:10:16.360
Facts kill humour, kids.

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:20.240
But the question is, did it work?

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:21.680
-No.
-Yes.

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:23.720
-Correct.
-Because everything else on the show hasn't.

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:29.200
Yes, 82% of the clouds produced rain
within a brief period after having been seeded.

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:31.040
Wow, that's very wet.

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:32.920
So it did work,

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:37.080
but nowadays you're not allowed to do that,
why not?

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:39.120
Some kind of treaty that says, 'Don't do that.'

00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:42.840
Weather modification treaties because it could
be used as an act of war?

00:10:42.840 --> 00:10:46.880
Ooh, you are absolutely right, it is the
Environmental Modification Convention.

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:48.000
Have a point.

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:49.240
Which was signed...

00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:50.760
The Weather-a-bugger-about-y Treaty.

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:55.080
Yes, the Weather-a-bugger-about-y Treaty.
that's really hard to say.

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:56.840
It's the Weather-a-bugger-about-y Treaty.

00:10:56.840 --> 00:10:59.600
The Weather-a-bugger-about-y Treaty.
and now we're going to a song, ♪ whoa... ♪

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:02.800
♪ The Weather-a-bugger-about-y Treaty ♪

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:08.200
Yes, it is a ban on weather modification
techniques

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:10.920
and on the use of herbicides in warfare.

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:13.280
When might that have come into use?

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:14.200
End of Vietnam.

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:18.280
Yeah, in 1977, Agent Orange
and everything was banned by that treaty.

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:20.400
Did they ban the modification of Kate Bush
as well?

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:22.200
How would you modify Kate Bush?

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:25.160
-Get rid of hailing.
-You're right, she can't be improved upon.

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:27.920
There is a link,
at the bottom of Operation Popeye.

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:30.040
Does it say never get involved
in a land war in Asia?

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:31.280
It says…

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:34.500
It says Project Storm Fury.

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:35.720
-F***!
-Yeah.

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:39.640
I want it, I want a badge, I want a hat with
it on, the whole thing, Project Storm Fury,

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:42.320
unless it killed a lot of people,
in which case I am less interested.

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:45.880
What was the US government trying to do
between '62 and '83

00:11:45.880 --> 00:11:48.480
with planes filled with silver iodide?

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:50.480
-Anger the weather.
-Un-anger the weather.

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:51.560
Yes.

00:11:52.680 --> 00:11:55.880
Make friends with weather
and then use it against them.

00:11:55.880 --> 00:11:59.220
Why would the US government, not the military;

00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:01.040
I nearly said US military,
but it's the government,

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:04.840
why would they want to modify the weather
on a large scale?

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:06.320
Get rid of the tornado belt.

00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:08.840
Ooh, it's close, it's not quite tornados

00:12:08.840 --> 00:12:11.080
but something else that's been hitting them
more lately.

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:12.080
Oh, hurricanes.

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:13.680
Yes, tropical cyclones.

00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:17.400
The idea was that they would fly an aircraft
into a cyclone.

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:18.760
Was it a Hurricane?

00:12:18.760 --> 00:12:20.360
Fly a Hurricane into a hurricane?

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:22.680
No.

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:25.040
(The Hurricane is a type of plane.)

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:26.080
Used in the olden days.

00:12:26.080 --> 00:12:29.360
Yes. No, it was a Lockheed P-3.

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:34.560
-Is that… is that a dull plane?
-Mmm.

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:37.320
I don't know if you were saying
that was a dull fact or it's a dull plane.

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:39.920
-Both.
-It's a dull plane being flown into a hurricane.

00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:41.840
What, you think it's just a way
to get rid of them?

00:12:41.840 --> 00:12:46.240
Some US army general, "We need more B1 Bombers,
they've got Swing Wings, God damn it.

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:48.000
"Fly the P-3s into a hurricane."

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:53.040
"Turn that recording of the meeting off,
we've heard enough."

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:57.400
Yeah, the idea was that it would just fly in.
Just fly in…!

00:12:57.400 --> 00:13:00.700
Presumably with Slim Pickens on the top
in his cowboy hat.

00:13:00.700 --> 00:13:01.880
"Wahoo!"

00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:07.400
And the answer is they probably didn't
make it work, but they did…

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:09.520
Well, we still have lots of hurricanes.

00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:11.880
Yeah, it probably wasn't actually going to
affect anything,

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:15.680
but they did get a positive outcome out of it,
what might that have been?

00:13:15.680 --> 00:13:16.800
Less P-3s.

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:18.560
Fewer P-3 Orions, yeah.

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:22.440
They absolutely found it didn't work but that
involves doing something, finding that out.

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:24.400
A massive amount of weather research.

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:28.820
Yes, that's absolutely right,
out of this attempt to seed the clouds,

00:13:28.820 --> 00:13:32.000
they found a huge amount of research that
helped them forecast future hurricanes.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:34.680
I was going to say this sounds very 50s,
but the fact they were actually trying,

00:13:34.680 --> 00:13:37.880
-it feels a bit later.
-1962 to 1983, have the last point.

00:13:37.880 --> 00:13:39.040
Yay!

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:43.640
And with that, congratulations,
Matt, you win the show.

00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:44.960
Yay!

00:13:44.960 --> 00:13:47.720
You win a vertical purple lead arse.

00:13:49.400 --> 00:13:51.480
It's a plumb plum plumbum bum.

00:13:53.800 --> 00:13:55.840
With that we say thank you to Chris Joel,

00:13:57.560 --> 00:13:58.720
to Gary Brannan,

00:13:59.320 --> 00:14:00.400
to Matt Gray.

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:02.800
I've been Tom Scott, we'll see you next time.

